WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.140
A street stall sells 2 snacks
an hour at a price of 8.

2
00:00:04.140 --> 00:00:06.150
That brings in 16.

3
00:00:06.150 --> 00:00:07.640
It wants a third customer,

4
00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:09.740
so it lowers its price to 6.

5
00:00:09.740 --> 00:00:12.430
The new customer pays 6.

6
00:00:12.430 --> 00:00:16.220
But the takings rise from 16 to just 18.

7
00:00:16.220 --> 00:00:17.610
Only 2 more.

8
00:00:17.610 --> 00:00:19.180
Where did the rest go?

9
00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:22.230
If a seller must cut its
price to sell one more,

10
00:00:22.230 --> 00:00:25.860
why does that extra sale
bring in less than the price?

11
00:00:25.860 --> 00:00:28.680
In this mission, you'll
build a revenue table:

12
00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:31.650
total, average and marginal revenue.

13
00:00:31.650 --> 00:00:35.710
Then you'll hunt for the price
where total revenue stops rising.

14
00:00:35.710 --> 00:00:38.920
Your mission: find out where
the missing money went.
